148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (In partnership with NDIGI and ND Delta, this competition brings together top quantitative and finance-focused students to build fully automated trading algorithms and deploy them in a live, exchange-simulated market. Using a Python SDK and a production-style matching engine developed by our trading competition lead, teams trade four assets, including an ETF with a defined basket relationship, against other participants, market-making bots, and noise traders. Over multiple short, high-intensity rounds, competitors design strategies such as ETF arbitrage, market making, momentum, and mean-reversion, all while managing P&L, fees, position limits, and real-time order-book dynamics.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (This competition will host over 100 top students with strong quantitative, analytical, and programming backgrounds. By designing and deploying trading algorithms in a live, fast-moving environment, participants demonstrate practical skills in strategy development, market reasoning, and real-time decision-making. The competition gives sponsors an early look at students who have hands-on experience building trading systems and ensures your firm is visible to a concentrated group of highly motivated quantitative finance candidates.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
